From 56bc8283869b9605bdea0840763ef3091c04383f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:50:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SHTSPELL: the in-shuttle aliases are spelled MInShuttle1 /
 MInShuttle2 (were MInShutte1 / MInShutte2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "是shuttle有些是拼錯 檔案都幫我直接修正 軟體也要改".
- cinitial.cpp InitialMotorName: SetAlias(11, "MInShuttle1"), SetAlias(12, "MInShuttle2"). golden's "不可以改成MInShuttle1"
  predates Steven 20250926's two-spelling TECH_PARA read/save (forms/fTeachPara.cpp: either alias finds [MInShuttle1] or
  [MInShutte1]); measured: D:\HT9045\system\teach.ini and runcfg\system\teach.ini hold only [MInShuttle1]/[MInShuttle2],
  so the single-motor teach values read and written stay the same; the two-motor items that use MOT[].Alias directly
  (fTeachPara.cpp :252 ...) now find [MInShuttle1] instead of a missing [MInShutte1].
- csystem.cpp: the local statics bHaveServoOnShutte1/2 -> bHaveServoOnShuttle1/2 (no behaviour change).
- Outside the repo, same day (backup D:\HT9045\_BACKUP_20260930_shuttle_spelling): D:\HT9045\system\Mot_Table.csv and
  machines\HT9050\Mot_Table.csv rows M11/M12 renamed. Old dated backups (system\teach_20260723.ini,
  system\2025052teach back up\teach.ini, machines\HT9050\Mot_Table.jimmy_20260924.csv) left as they were.
Syntax check rc=0 (cinitial.cpp, csystem.cpp); no test names the old spelling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cinitial.cpp |  6 +++---
 csystem.cpp  | 26 +++++++++++++-------------
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cinitial.cpp b/cinitial.cpp
index 95b1a11..f54d2fe 100644
--- a/cinitial.cpp
+++ b/cinitial.cpp
@@ -3301,7 +3301,7 @@ void InitialHeaterDoor()
 //  (golden :3122 carries the warning comment), MInRotateKit->"MInRotate",
 //  MOutRotateKit->"MOutRotate" (:3152).  The alias is the Teaching-file key;
 //  renaming it breaks teach-data lookup on a real machine.  Preserved verbatim,
-//  typo and all.
+//  typo and all.   [AI(W906-SHTSPELL) 20260930: the two shuttle aliases ARE corrected now (EastSun) -- see :3321; MInRotate/MOutRotate unchanged]
 //
 //  Translator: AI(W906-GA2-IMN) 20260809
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -3318,8 +3318,8 @@ void InitialMotorName()
     MOT[MInArmZF      ].SetAlias(  8, "MInArmZF");
     MOT[MInArmZG      ].SetAlias(  9, "MInArmZG");
     MOT[MInArmZH      ].SetAlias( 10, "MInArmZH");
-    MOT[MInShuttle1   ].SetAlias( 11, "MInShutte1");                            //不可以改成MInShuttle1, 會造成Teaching異常
-    MOT[MInShuttle2   ].SetAlias( 12, "MInShutte2");
+    MOT[MInShuttle1   ].SetAlias( 11, "MInShuttle1");                           //不可以改成MInShuttle1, 會造成Teaching異常   //AI(W906-SHTSPELL) 20260930: EastSun「是shuttle有些是拼錯 檔案都幫我直接修正 軟體也要改」-- was "MInShutte1". The warning predates Steven 20250926's two-spelling read/save (forms/fTeachPara.cpp TECH_PARA::ReadFromFile / SaveToFile: an alias of either spelling finds [MInShuttle1] or [MInShutte1]); this machine's teach.ini (system\ and runcfg\system\) has only [MInShuttle1]/[MInShuttle2], so the teach values read and written are the same ones as before. Mot_Table.csv M11/M12 renamed the same day
+    MOT[MInShuttle2   ].SetAlias( 12, "MInShuttle2");                           //AI(W906-SHTSPELL) 20260930: was "MInShutte2" (see the line above)
     MOT[MTestY1       ].SetAlias( 13, "MTestY1");
     MOT[MTestZ1       ].SetAlias( 14, "MTestZ1");
     MOT[MTestZ2       ].SetAlias( 15, "MTestZ2");
